---
pagination:
  data: collections.categories
  size: 1
  alias: category
permalink: "/{{ site.categoryBase or 'category' }}/{{ category.name | urlencode }}/"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#
  A category archive per category in use, at the URL the CMS serves one from —
  under `site.categoryBase`, which the settings screen mirrors into site.json.

  Eleventy builds collections from `tags` on its own; `categories` is an
  ordinary data key to it, so the example config exposes `collections.categories`
  and this is the template that turns it into pages. It lives in the fixtures
  rather than in the package so `test/eleventy.test.ts` can prove the URLs match.
#}
<h1>Filed under &ldquo;{{ category.name }}&rdquo;</h1>
<ul>
  {% for post in category.posts %}
  <li><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a></li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
